## Context

Follow-up from [[2028]] required by .claude/rules/script-io.md Migration.
The occurrence selector touches existing legacy CLI readers; rewriting their
multi-command parsers would expand the scientific correction's scope.

## Scope

Migrate the shared-I/O contracts of corpus_rel_view.py, corpus_icf_stage2.py,
corpus_rel_discipline_catchup.py, corpus_icf_import.py and
corpus_rel_repec_prefilter.py without changing their scientific behavior.

## Test

Existing command/parser fixtures plus output argument contract checks.

## Exit criteria

- These five legacy CLIs use parse_io_args/validate_io as applicable and declare
  required explicit output or documented multi-output directory arguments.
- Preserve existing parser commands, file outputs, model/budget behavior and
  ordinary scientific selection; no data regeneration or paid calls.
- Meaningful parser tests and the required project gate pass; no new bypasses
  in the I/O ratchet.
